+# Browser Use: Persona dual-loop adapter
+
+L independently watches browser screenshots/page state and remains available
+for user conversation. R supplies Browser Use's action decisions, extraction,
+judging and other task inference. Browser Use retains its native task loop,
+tools, history and stop/pause handling. Both use the same Persona chat endpoint.
+
+## Installation
+
+Install the bundled shared package and this source checkout:
+
+```bash
+uv venv
+uv pip install -e ../persona-lanes -e .
+uv run browser-use install
+```
+
+```python
+import asyncio
+import os
+from persona_lanes import LaneConfig, PersonaLanes
+from browser_use.llm.persona import persona_agent
+from browser_use.persona.observer import ObserverSettings
+
+async def main():
+    async with PersonaLanes(LaneConfig(
+        base_url=os.environ['PERSONA_BASE_URL'],  # origin, without /v1
+        api_key=os.environ['PERSONA_API_KEY'],
+    )) as lanes:
+        agent = persona_agent(
+            lanes=lanes,
+            task='Open the supplied website and complete the requested task',
+            observer_settings=ObserverSettings(
+                sample_interval=0.75, inference_interval=2.0,
+            ),
+        )
+        # run() starts the native task loop AND background L observation.
+        work = asyncio.create_task(agent.run())
+        try:
+            async for text in agent.conversation([
+                {'role':'user', 'content':'Tell me what you can currently see.'}
+            ]):
+                print(text, end='', flush=True)
+            await work
+        finally:
+            if not work.done():
+                work.cancel()
+                await asyncio.gather(work, return_exceptions=True)
+
+asyncio.run(main())
+```
+
+No UI is required for observation to run. An application may connect its text
+or voice input to agent.conversation() independently. This adapter transports
+text; it does not implement microphone capture or TTS. The PersonaLanes client
+is owned/closed by the caller and can also serve other authorized connections.
+
+## How the loops interact
+
+- A sampler reads the focused target through CDP with focus=False. It reads
+  visible text/form state and captures a JPEG without replacing the DOM or
+  selector cache owned by the native Browser Use action loop.
+- A separate L task inspects changed frames. It retains only the latest pending
+  frame, limits request cadence, cancels superseded DOM observations, and
+  publishes bounded, timestamped observations. Page instructions are treated
+  as untrusted evidence, never as system/task instructions.
+- R receives an available matching L observation when it next requests inference.
+  It never waits for L. A result arriving after R starts generating is used on
+  a later request; this API cannot splice new tokens into an existing generation.
+- The adapter samples state around native context preparation and just before
+  executing a decision. Changed URL/target/visible DOM/form state causes a normal
+  step error/retry and fresh planning. Browser Use's own action guards remain.
+  One action is allowed per refreshed decision to avoid stale action batches.
+- Animation-only image changes refresh observations but do not by themselves
+  invalidate R's DOM decision. This is a bounded semantic guard, not a guarantee
+  against every possible visual or instantaneous browser change.
+- Closing/cancelling the agent closes observation tasks and their streams.
+  Cancelling a conversation alone does not stop the browser task. Native
+  stop/pause semantics still apply; in-flight tools need their native cancellation.
+
+## Inference connection requirements
+
+The same POST /v1/chat/completions receives X-Sawii-Lane and sawii_lane (L or R),
+plus a shared X-Sawii-Session-Id / sawii_session_id. Persona must acknowledge
+X-Sawii-Lane in responses, accept screenshot content in L messages, and allow
+L/R calls to overlap. User conversation and L observation also need appropriately
+isolated simultaneous L requests if both must remain immediately responsive.
+The SDK has no shared request lock; it cannot remove a server/provider lock.
+
+Draft PR #118 is the architectural baseline. When inspected at commit
+7b33380aed447916faa9a47ced2fa5d4c500c215 it still lists live inference routing
+and concurrency as unfinished. This archive does not merge, deploy, or claim to
+complete that backend work. It does not create the mirrored secondary Cline.
+
+Sampling default: at most one frame per 0.75 s; L inference at most once per
+2 seconds after a previous observation finishes, and only for changed frames.
+Observation calls incur model/memory work under the backend's existing behavior.
+Use agent.persona_observer.last_error to inspect observer availability.
+
+## Validation
+
+31 focused tests passed across the existing lane adapters/backend-contract tests
+and the new observation tests. The 9 Browser Use-specific tests included here
+cover concurrent L observation during a blocked R request, latest-frame handling,
+stale-action rejection, note expiry, resource cleanup, read-only CDP capture,
+native-provider serialization, and delegation to the native Agent lifecycle
+using test doubles. Also verified construction of the installed real Browser Use
+Agent with the Persona provider. Formatting/lint pass for added source.
+
+Chromium could not be installed: the browser download returned an invalid ZIP.
+Consequently real browser execution and live Persona inference remain unverified.
+To run the included focused tests from this checkout:
+
+```bash
+uv pip install pytest pytest-asyncio
+uv run python -m pytest -q -o addopts='' tests/persona --confcutdir=tests/persona
+```
+
+Upstream source commit is recorded in the archive manifest; upstream MIT license
+is retained. Added source: browser_use/llm/persona.py, browser_use/persona/.
